            "ABC velocity slotting classifies stock-keeping units (SKUs) based on their pick frequency, pick volume, and physical dimensions rather than simple sales revenue. In classic Pareto analysis, Class A SKUs typically represent the top twenty percent of items that generate seventy to eighty percent of total pick travel transactions; Class B SKUs account for thirty percent of items generating fifteen percent of transactions; and Class C SKUs comprise the remaining fifty percent of slow-moving items generating only five to ten percent of picks.",
